course: dictionary
lesson: 1817
title: Clumsy: more than tripping
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clumsy has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one the writer wants. «Reading your work aloud helps you hear missing words, clumsy sentences and tense slips.» Here a clumsy sentence is one that is awkward and does not flow well, so it needs rewriting.
explain: «Toad keeps his temper, though he finds their jokes poor and clumsy.» Poor and clumsy both describe how well the jokes are done, not how someone moves. Ask yourself: is a person moving badly, or is something done without skill?
explain: «People hope robots and AI will help with boring chores, but real home robots are still clumsy and expensive.» Here clumsy describes machines that are hard to use or control well. Try your meaning in the sentence: hard to control, not very skilful. If it fits, you have it.
fact: Clumsy means awkward, careless or not done well.
fact: Clumsy can describe a person who moves badly and often drops, bumps or breaks things.
fact: Clumsy can describe something big, heavy and hard to move or use.
fact: Clumsy can describe words or actions done without skill, as in «a clumsy apology».
fact: Everyone can be clumsy sometimes, especially when tired or growing fast.
exercise: «People hope robots and AI will help with boring chores, but real home robots are still clumsy and expensive.» What does clumsy mean here? | Quick and cheap | *Hard to use or control, not very skilful | Bright and colourful | Very kind and friendly
exercise: Ella says clumsy only means someone falls over. Is she right? | Yes, it only ever means falling over | No, it means very quick | *No, it can also describe words or actions done without skill, like «a clumsy apology» | Yes, it means tidy and neat
exercise: «On land penguins waddle like clumsy toys, but the moment they dive they shoot through the water like torpedoes.» Find and copy one word that means awkward or not graceful. | shoot | water | *clumsy | torpedoes
test: «Reading your work aloud helps you hear clumsy sentences.» What is a clumsy sentence? | A sentence written in pencil | *An awkward sentence that needs rewriting | A sentence that is too long to read | A sentence with a question mark
test: In the phrase «a clumsy attempt», what does clumsy suggest? | An attempt that is very expensive | An attempt that is very fast | *An attempt done without skill | An attempt made only by a giant
exam: Mia says clumsy is only about feet. Which sentence shows the meaning is wider? | Clumsy means the same as clean | Clumsy only describes animals | *Clumsy can describe a heavy, hard-to-use object or a poorly done apology | Clumsy means fast and quiet
